license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Karatum
    given-names: Mustafa
    affiliation: Independent researcher
abstract: >-
  An interactive FLRW background simulator with adaptive numerical integration,
  conservative dark-matter transfers, conditional asymptotic continuation
  (including proof-based continuation of CPL dark-energy laws), exactly located
  cosmic events, de Sitter horizon thermodynamics, astrophysical tracer
  approximations, uncertainty sampling and versioned observational provenance.
  Verified by analytic benchmarks, an independent SciPy reference, a golden
  master of example outputs and property-based tests. A research software
  preview, not a unique forecast of the actual cosmic fate or an externally
  peer-reviewed solver.
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - FLRW
  - dark energy
  - numerical simulation
  - reproducibility
  - scientific visualization
  - Friedmann equations
  - research software
